# kaizen — per-dir gitignore.
#
# Ignores ephemeral kaizen state (cache/, hooks/, trace/, daemon
# socket, etc.). Durable workflow artifacts under workflow/ stay
# tracked: progress.md (architecture log) and backlog.{json,md}.
# This keeps the rule local to .kaizen/ so the repo root's
# .gitignore stays project-focused.
#
# Note: audit reports live at .kaizen/workflow/audits/ — covered by
# the broad `!workflow/**` whitelist below, then re-ignored via the
# trailing `workflow/audits/` rule because they're auto-regenerated
# per `kaizen audit` run, not durable artifacts.
#
# Runtime artifacts (state.json, deletions.jsonl, snapshot.md) live
# under workflow/ but ARE ephemeral — explicitly re-ignored via the
# trailing rules below so the broad `!workflow/**` whitelist doesn't
# pick them up. They regenerate every workflow run.

*
!.gitignore
!workflow/
!workflow/**

# Re-ignore ephemeral runtime state under workflow/ that the broad
# whitelist above would otherwise pick up.
workflow/state.json
workflow/deletions.jsonl
workflow/snapshot.md

# Audit reports — auto-regenerated by `kaizen audit`. The earlier
# tracked report (2026-05-17T01-45-46Z-repo.md) stays tracked because
# git ignores ignore rules for already-tracked files.
workflow/audits/
